---
source: crates/modde-cli/tests/cli_help_snapshots.rs
expression: "without_optional_commands(stdout(&[]))"
---

--- stderr ---
NixOS-native game mod manager

Usage: modde [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  library     Owned game catalogue and saved per-installation launch settings
  profile     Manage profiles
  lock        Export, sign, verify, and import portable modde.lock files
  config      Inspect and set modde configuration (including the database backend)
  play        Switch profile, deploy mods, and launch the game
  perf        Capture and compare local performance telemetry
  deploy      Deploy mods for the active or specified profile
  hot-deploy  Patch one cosmetic mod into the live VFS without a full redeploy
  rollback    Rollback to the previous deployment
  install     Install mods from various sources
  mod         Manage individual mods (remove, diagnose unknown-type dossiers)
  verify      Verify installed file integrity
  nexus       Nexus Mods account management
  stock       Manage vanilla game snapshots
  fomod       FOMOD installer utilities
  save        Manage save file assignments
  update      Check for mod updates from Nexus
  patcher     Configure and run profile-scoped patcher pipeline stages
  tool        Run external tools with overwrite capture
  nxm         Handle nxm:// download links from Nexus Mods
  wabbajack   Browse, download, and generate Home Manager snippets for Wabbajack modlists
  scan        Scan game directory for installed mods
  collisions  Analyse mod collisions and suggest optimisations
  doctor      Diagnose profiles and crash logs with grounded evidence
  bisect      Binary-search enabled mods to isolate a crash or performance regression
  export      Export mod list to CSV
  backup      Manage mod and plugin order backups
  detect      Detect installed games across Steam and Heroic launchers
  game        Manage user-defined games
  instance    Manage modde instances (multiple data directories)
  exec        Manage named launch targets (`xEdit`, `BodySlide`, `FNIS`, etc.)
  skill       Install and update modde-maintained Codex skills
  import      Import existing TOML profiles into the database
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --data-dir <DATA_DIR>          Override data directory (default: ~/.local/share/modde or $`MODDE_DATA_DIR`) [env: MODDE_DATA_DIR=]
      --config-dir <CONFIG_DIR>      Override the base configuration directory used by modde and its session journal
      --heap-profile <HEAP_PROFILE>  Write a DHAT heap profile. Requires the `heap-profile` cargo feature [env: MODDE_HEAP_PROFILE=]
  -h, --help                         Print help
  -V, --version                      Print version
